{{Quote|It ''is'' a form of barley&mdash;specifically ''Vratixia renanicus''. Originally cultivated on ''Thyferra'', it is a key ingredient of ''bacta'' alongside alazhi and kavam.|[[Jedi]] [[Estala Maru]]|<ref name="THR 2" />}}
'''Thyferra''' was a [[planet]] located in the [[Inner Rim Territories]], lying on the [[Rimma Trade Route]]. It was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Vratix]] [[species]], who invented the substance [[bacta]] and eventually became addicted to it. When [[human]]s who [[Colonist|settled]] on the planet discovered the bacta, they exploited the species' addiction and sold the substance to the public. The [[barley]] known as ''[[Vratixia renanicus]]'' was also [[Farm|cultivated]] on the planet. The [[First Order]] military regime later gained control of Thyferra, and following the regime's defeat at the [[Battle of Exegol]] in [[35 ABY]], the planet was in [[Uprising on Thyferra|open rebellion]] against it.

==Description==
{{Quote|Bet you didn't know this slimy-yet-soothin' substance was first created on the Inner Rim planet Thyferra usin' a native stream of Vratixian barley, did ya?|Strono Tuggs, regarding the bacta substance, ''The Ultimate Cookbook''|<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref>}}
Thyferra was a terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="GE2">{{EncyclopediaCite|General Equipment (2)}}</ref> in the [[Jaso sector]]'s [[Thyferra system]]<ref name="Appendix" /> within the [[Inner Rim Territories]]. The world was situated in grid square L-14 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]]. The [[Rimma Trade Route]] [[hyperspace route]] connected it to the [[Yag'Dhul system|Yag'Dhul]] and [[Ghorman system]]s.<ref name="TFABG" />

==History==
{{Quote|Incoming freighter from Thyferra. Clear docking bay 34.|A coordinator at Mirogana Spaceport|audio=Thyferra-Outlaws.flac|<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>}}
[[File:VratixianBarley-2021THR2.jpg|thumb|right|300px|The ''Vratixia renanicus'' barley was cultivated on Thyferra.]]
By the [[time]] of the [[High Republic Era]],<ref name="THR P1 Artbook">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The High Republic: Volume I]]''</ref> the substance [[bacta]] was<ref name="GE2" /> newly<ref name="THR P1 Artbook" /> invented by Thyferra's [[Homeworld|native]] [[Vratix]] [[species]]. They became so addicted to it that they were compelled to produce more. [[Human]]s eventually arrived and [[Colonist|settled]] on the planet, discovering bacta's healing properties. The settlers took advantage of the Vratix's addiction to bacta by encouraging them to produce more of it, selling the substance to the general public. While the settlers [[Currency|profited]] greatly, the natives became an [[Slavery|enslaved]] labor force.<ref name="GE2" />

By [[232 BBY]],<ref name="THR 2 Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[The High Republic (2021) 2|''The High Republic'' (2021) 2]] to [[232 BBY]].</ref> a type of [[barley]] named ''[[Vratixia renanicus]]'' was [[Farm|cultivated]] on Thyferra and was a key ingredient in bacta.<ref name="THR 2" /> At some point by around the same [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="YJADate">{{YJADate|211B}}</ref> the [[Marlaa Jinara's junkyard|junkyard]] owner [[Marlaa Jinara]] spent time adventuring on Thyferra.<ref name="TJJ">{{YJA|The Jumping Jetpack}}</ref> In 232 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]],<ref name="YJADate" /> after the [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi youngling]] [[Kai Brightstar]] asked for a story about her experiences, she conceded and inquired if he had heard of the world.<ref name="TJJ" /> The natives of Thyferra created the [[Bacta Slush]] beverage at one point to remedy internal maladies.<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook" /> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> a [[freighter]] from Thyferra was announced to be approaching [[Mirogana Spaceport]] in the [[city]] of [[Mirogana]] on the [[moon]] [[Toshara]].<ref name="Outlaws" />

By [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Flight of Ash Angels Date">"[[The Impossible Flight of Ash Angels]]" takes place concurrently to the events of {{Film|VI}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[4 ABY]], and also establishes that the [[Bacta Cartel]] was active by the time of the story.</ref> the [[Bacta Cartel]] operated on the world.<ref name="Incredibuilds" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="MandoDate">{{MandoVGDate}}</ref> Thyferra was part of the [[New Republic]]'s territories.<ref name="MandoVG" /> At some point afterward, the [[First Order military|forces]] of the [[First Order]], formed from remnants of the [[Galactic Empire]] after their defeat, eventually took control of Thyferra.<ref name="Final Order SWE" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Starcruiserdate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]] to [[34 ABY]].</ref> the ''[[Halcyon]]'', [[Chandrila Star Line]]'s [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|Star Cruiser]], passed by Thyferra during a cruise from the [[Core Worlds]]' [[Chandrila system]] to the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. A partial [[Star map|map]] of [[the galaxy]] indicating the planet's position was displayed on several [[Viewscreen|screens]] aboard the [[Star Cruiser|starship]].<ref name="GS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref> At some point between 34 ABY and [[35 ABY]],<ref name="UltimateCookbookDate">{{UltimateCookbookDate}}</ref> [[Artiodac]] [[chef]] [[Strono Tuggs]] undertook a culinary tour of the [[galaxy]]. He consumed a Bacta Slush and included a recipe for the beverage, documenting its taste and origin, in his [[Book|cookbook]], ''[[The Ultimate Cookbook]]'',<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook" /> published in 35 ABY.<ref name="UltimateCookbookDate">{{UltimateCookbookDate}}</ref> Following the First Order's defeat at the [[Battle of Exegol]]<ref name="Final Order SWE" /> of 35 ABY,<ref name="Eulogy for Snap">{{StoryCite|story=A Eulogy for Snap|book=Star Wars (2020) 25}}</ref> many worlds entered an [[Uprising against the First Order|open rebellion]] against the regime. One such [[Uprising on Thyferra|uprising]] took place on Thyferra after [[Uprising on Coruscant|similar]] [[Uprising on Corellia|revolts]] on the prominent worlds of [[Coruscant]] and [[Corellia]] had occurred.<ref name="Final Order SWE" />

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|Bacta may be good for healin' what's on the surface, but it prob'ly ain't somethin' you should drink to fix what ails you deep on the inside. Good thing the fine folks on Thyferra came up with a little somethin' for that, too&mdash;an icy, creamy, fruit-filled slush that's sure to have you feelin' better in no time flat.|Strono Tuggs on Bacta Slush, ''The Ultimate Cookbook''|<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook" />}}
Thyferra was home to the [[insectoid]] Vratix, who were exploited to sell bacta by humans who later settled there.<ref name="GE2" /> One human who hailed from the planet, [[Arvel Crynyd]], was a [[Z-95 Headhunter]] [[pilot]] for the Bacta Cartel before joining the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]].<ref name="HC 75">{{HelmetCollectionCite|75|Weapons & Uniforms}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:BTMF52.png|thumb|right|200px|In the current canon, Thyferra was first introduced via mention on a map in ''Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon'' 52.]]
Thyferra was first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] on a map featured in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 52|fifty-second issue]] of [[De Agostini]]'s ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF 52">{{BuildFalconCite|52|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> published around [[December 30]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|52}}</ref> The planet made its first [[in-universe]] appearance via a map viewable in [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], an immersive roleplaying experience at [[W:c:disney:Walt Disney World Resort|Walt Disney World Resort]] in [[Wikipedia:Florida|Florida]]<ref name="GS" /> that opened to the public on [[March 1]], [[2022]],<ref name="31 Things">{{SW|url=news/31-things-we-learned-about-star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=31 Things We Learned in an Exclusive Preview of ''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser|nolive=1}}</ref> and had its final voyage from [[September 28]] to [[September 30|30]], [[2023]].<ref name="StarcruiserClosure">{{Disney|subdomain=disneyworld|domain=go.com|url=destinations/star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser}}</ref>

In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, [[Thyferra/Legends|Thyferra]] was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game|roleplaying game]] article "[[The Business of Bacta]]," written by [[Michael Kogge]] and published in the [[Star Wars Adventure Journal 3|third issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars Adventure Journal]]'' magazine in [[August]] [[1994]].<ref name="The Business of Bacta">{{JournalCite|3|The Business of Bacta}}</ref> The [[Planet/Legends|planet]] subsequently made its first appearance in ''[[X-Wing: The Bacta War]]'', a [[1997]] novel written by [[Michael A. Stackpole]] as the fourth entry in the [[Star Wars: X-Wing (novel series)|''Star Wars: X-Wing'']] novel series.<ref name="Bacta War">''[[X-Wing: The Bacta War]]''</ref>

